  "raw": " and Giant Bomb. Even topping criticisms that had been leveled even before the game’s release. Zelda fans would go on to compare the game to such titles as Zelda II: The Adventure of Link, A Link to the Past, and Ocarina of Time. When the Wii was released three generations later, the grass was trimmed even further when the GameCube version of the game was released and came out on top with a 95/100 score for both 1UP.com and GameSpot. You now have the opportunity to return to Hyrule and defeat Hyrule’s monster, Ganon, to claim Zelda’s Triforce of Power before it’s lost forever… You hear that monsters, nightmares are not yet dead. Soon you will find them wherever you look.",
  "serialized": "and Giant Bomb. Even topping criticisms that had been leveled even before the game’s release. Zelda fans would go on to compare the game to such titles as Zelda II: The Adventure of Link, A Link to the Past, and Ocarina of Time. When the Wii was released three generations later, the grass was trimmed even further when the GameCube version of the game was released and came out on top with a 95/100 score for both 1UP.com and GameSpot. You now have the opportunity to return to Hyrule and defeat Hyrule’s monster, Ganon, to claim Zelda’s Triforce of Power before it’s lost forever… You hear that monsters, nightmares are not yet dead. Soon you will find them wherever you look.",
